  "review": [
    "Body fit is a shared policy. A fixed 32-card semantic/density refinement cohort selects numeric candidates; full 268 verification retains every regression. The legacy layout supplies only a content-derived maximum line count. The new metrics then fit down to that budget without per-card exceptions.",
    "The P/T cohort contains all 148 ordinary printed stat fields. Font/size/position comparisons use the same source family and fixed masks. Both font alternatives must be actually loaded; no missing-font fallbacks count as candidates.",
    "Fractional metrics are explicit for measurement, request replay and painting. The painter still retains browser rasterization, including bounded HTML/Offscreen differences; numerical layout precision does not imply pixel identity between backends.",
    "Residuals remain visible. Native adoption parity and improved indices do not certify scan poses, missing art spills, exact printing data, all modern donor sets or M21 completion.",
    "The properly loaded 2016 P/T candidate was rejected: Kinetic Augur\u2019s */4 falls 34.93 points. The existing font with precise metrics and .97 size wins the shared cohort. Earlier wrong-family prototype trials are not evidence."
  ],
